From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: retain the G725 name in downstream core-count naming

Mesa 27 already selects distinct G725 and G925 model rows using core count
and ray-intersection features. Preserve those upstream rows instead of
combining their names. Only retain the explicit Mali-G725 spelling in the
downstream Vulkan core-count naming helper introduced by csf-v11/131.

Cosmetic only; Vulkan deviceName is unchanged for every core count.
Build-only; no device test.
---
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
index 6a79a73..a6d85a4 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
@@ -1221,7 +1221,7 @@ panvk_marketing_name(const struct pan_model *model, unsigned core_count)
                                : "Mali-G620";
    case PAN_PROD_ID(13, 8, 0):
       return core_count >= 10 ? "Mali-G925-Immortalis"
-             : core_count >= 6 ? model->name
+             : core_count >= 6 ? "Mali-G725"
                                : "Mali-G625";
    default:
       return model->name;
